<title>KAZAKHSTAN: D. Telekom spurned in Kazakh telcoms deal.</title>
<headline>D. Telekom spurned in Kazakh telcoms deal.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A senior Kazakh official cited by state news agency Khabar-Press on Monday said a deal to sell a 49 percent share in the republic's state telecoms monopoly to Deutsche Telekom AG had fallen through.</p>
<p>&quot;A telegram was sent to the German side (from the Kazakh government) in which the heads of Deutsche Telekom were notified that talks to conclude the contract were over,&quot; said the agency, quoting Saribay Kalmurzayev, the powerful head of the State Property Committee.</p>
</text>
